###
App Intents define actions


An[App Intent](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appintents/appintent) describes an action, the inputs it needs, and the code that performs it.


For example, an “Add Food Item to Cart” intent might accept a food item and a quantity. Your Swift code then updates the cart.


App Entities and App Intents are established parts of Apple’s frameworks. The new tool support builds on that work, giving Siri AI access to eligible custom actions.


```text
struct    AddItemToCartIntent  :    AppIntent    {
static    let    title  :    LocalizedStringResource   =  "Add Item to Cart"


@Parameter  (  title  :    "Food Item"  )    var    foodItem  :    FoodItemEntity
@Parameter  (  title  :    "Cart"  )    var    cart  :    CartEntity


static    var    parameterSummary  :    some    ParameterSummary    {
Summary  (  "Add \(  \ .  $ foodItem  ) to \(  \ .  $ cart  )"  )
}


func    perform  (  )    async    throws   ->  some    IntentResult    {
// add foodItem code goes here
return    .result  (  )
}
}
```


