##
App Intents and the ToolIntent Protocol


Your App Intents can easily conform to the[ToolIntent](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appintents/toolintent) protocol by adding the` @AppIntent(.tool)` macro. Doing this will make your tools available to Siri AI under certain circumstances (more on that below).


This is why if you've already built out your App Intents, you've done most of the work.


```text
@AppIntent  (  .tool  )    // Make your App Intent a tool with this Macro
struct    AddItemToCartIntent  :    AppIntent    {
static    let    title  :    LocalizedStringResource   =  "Add Item to Cart"


@Parameter  (  title  :    "Cart"  )    var    cart  :    CartEntity


static    var    parameterSummary  :    some    ParameterSummary    {
Summary  (  "Add \(  \ .  $ foodItem  ) to \(  \ .  $ cart  )"  )
}


func    perform  (  )    async    throws   ->  some    IntentResult    {
// add foodItem code goes here
return    .result  (  )
}
}
```


